The function open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle.recover_json_object fails to distinguish Reply A (~~~json\n{\"a\":1}\n~~~\n{\"b\":2}) from Reply B ({\"b\":2}) as its documented rule requires, because its fence-matching regex recognizes only triple backticks and not tilde fences, causing it to return {\"b\":2} for both replies instead of {\"a\":1} for A and {\"b\":2} for B.